<PolicyLayout
  title="Terms of Service | ATL TV Mount"
  description="Terms of Service for ATL TV Mount, operated by Northline Mounting Services LLC."
>
  <p class="policy-kicker">Legal</p>
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: September 22, 2026</p>

  <div class="policy-content">
    <p>
      These Terms of Service govern services provided by
      <strong>ATL TV Mount, operated by Northline Mounting Services LLC</strong>
      (“ATL TV Mount,” “Northline,” “we,” “us,” or “our”).
    </p>

    <p>
      By requesting, booking, or receiving services from us, you agree to these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Services</h2>

    <p>
      We provide TV mounting and related installation services, which may include
      wall mounting, bracket installation, cable concealment, soundbar installation,
      equipment placement, and other related work agreed upon with the customer.
    </p>

    <p>
      The exact scope of work may depend on the TV, wall construction, mounting location,
      equipment, accessibility, and conditions found at the service location.
    </p>

    <h2>Estimates and Pricing</h2>

    <p>
      Prices provided through our website, calculator, text messages, photographs,
      phone conversations, or other communications are estimates based on the information
      available at the time.
    </p>

    <p>
      If site conditions, equipment, wall construction, requested work, or other material
      circumstances differ from the information originally provided, the final price may change.
    </p>

    <p>
      We will communicate material changes to the scope or price before performing
      additional work whenever reasonably practicable.
    </p>

    <h2>Booking and Scheduling</h2>

    <p>
      Appointment times may be provided as arrival windows rather than exact arrival times.
      Travel conditions, earlier appointments, access issues, or other circumstances may affect
      arrival timing.
    </p>

    <p>
      Customers should provide accurate contact information, service address, and relevant
      installation details when booking.
    </p>

    <h2>Cancellation and Rescheduling</h2>

    <p>
      You may cancel or reschedule an appointment by contacting us.
    </p>

    <p>
      We currently do not require a booking deposit or charge a cancellation or rescheduling fee.
    </p>

    <p>
      We may reschedule or cancel an appointment when reasonably necessary because of
      technician availability, unsafe conditions, severe weather, equipment issues,
      scheduling conflicts, or circumstances outside our reasonable control.
    </p>

    <h2>Payment</h2>

    <p>
      Payment is generally due after the agreed work has been completed.
    </p>

    <p>We may accept:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Major credit or debit cards processed through Square</li>
      <li>Zelle</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Card payments are processed by Square. Zelle payments are processed through
      participating financial institutions.
    </p>

    <h2>Customer Responsibilities</h2>

    <p>
      Customers are responsible for providing reasonable access to the installation area
      and for informing us of known conditions that could affect the work.
    </p>

    <p>
      This may include known plumbing, electrical wiring, unusual wall construction,
      concealed utilities, previous wall damage, or other conditions that may not be
      reasonably visible before work begins.
    </p>

    <p>
      If customer-supplied equipment, mounts, cables, hardware, or accessories are used,
      the customer is responsible for ensuring that those products are appropriate for
      the intended equipment and installation.
    </p>

    <h2>Five-Year Installation Workmanship Warranty</h2>

    <p>
      We provide a <strong>five-year workmanship warranty</strong> on the mounting work
      performed by us.
    </p>

    <p>
      During the warranty period, if a TV mounting failure occurs because of our installation
      workmanship, we will evaluate the installation and provide an appropriate remedy.
    </p>

    <p>
      This warranty is intended to cover the secure attachment of the TV resulting from
      our installation. It does not cover failures or damage caused by circumstances outside
      our installation workmanship, including:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Defective or inappropriate customer-supplied mounts or hardware</li>
      <li>Structural deterioration or hidden defects in the wall or building</li>
      <li>Alteration, removal, adjustment, or reinstallation by another person</li>
      <li>Impact, misuse, abuse, or accidental damage</li>
      <li>Water, fire, severe weather, structural movement, or similar external events</li>
      <li>Failure of the TV, mount, accessory, or other manufactured product itself</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      To request warranty service, contact us at
      <a href="mailto:info@atltvmount.com">info@atltvmount.com</a>
      or <a href="tel:+14704709331">(470) 470-9331</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Photographs of Completed Work</h2>

    <p>
      We may photograph completed installation work for documentation, portfolio,
      website, social media, Google Business Profile, advertising, and other marketing purposes.
    </p>

    <p>
      Customers may request that their installation not be photographed.
    </p>

    <p>
      We do not intentionally publish customer names, street addresses, personal documents,
      people, or other clearly identifying personal information in installation photographs
      without separate permission.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you do not want your installation photographed, please notify us before or during
      the appointment.
    </p>

    <h2>SMS and MMS Messaging Terms</h2>

    <p>
      ATL TV Mount may send SMS or MMS messages to customers who initiate a text conversation
      or otherwise provide valid consent to receive service-related messages.
    </p>

    <p>Messages may include:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Responses to customer questions</li>
      <li>Estimates and service discussions</li>
      <li>Appointment confirmations and reminders</li>
      <li>Scheduling and arrival updates</li>
      <li>Service-related follow-ups</li>
      <li>Responses regarding photographs or installation information</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      We do not use this messaging program for unsolicited marketing, promotional campaigns,
      newsletters, or mass advertising.
    </p>

    <p>Message frequency varies.</p>
    <p>Message and data rates may apply.</p>

    <p>
      Reply <strong>STOP</strong> at any time to opt out of SMS/MMS messages.
      Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for assistance or contact
      <a href="mailto:info@atltvmount.com">info@atltvmount.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Consent to receive SMS/MMS messages is voluntary and is not a condition of purchasing services.
    </p>

    <p>
      Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.
    </p>

    <p>
      Information about how we handle mobile information and messaging consent is available
      in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Products and Services</h2>

    <p>
      TVs, mounting brackets, cables, accessories, streaming devices, and other products
      manufactured or supplied by third parties are subject to their manufacturers’ terms,
      specifications, and warranties.
    </p>

    <p>
      We are not responsible for manufacturing defects or failures of third-party products
      that are unrelated to our installation workmanship.
    </p>

    <h2>Property and Installation Conditions</h2>

    <p>
      Installation work may involve drilling, fastening, cutting, or making openings in walls
      or other surfaces when required for the requested service.
    </p>

    <p>
      We take reasonable care when performing work, but concealed conditions may not always
      be detectable before work begins.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of Responsibility</h2>

    <p>
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, Northline Mounting Services LLC is not
      responsible for indirect, incidental, or consequential losses arising from circumstances
      outside the scope of the services we agreed to perform.
    </p>

    <p>
      Nothing in these Terms is intended to exclude or limit responsibility that cannot
